From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi7: 057 允许从 /lib/firmware 加载 WM 固件

Every image we can try today is compiled into the driver, so testing another
patch or RAM code means another full build.  The packaged image already
carries the casan variants next to the plain ones, and the plain ones are
byte-identical to the built-in arrays, so the only thing missing is a way to
point the MCU loader at a file.

diag_use_fw_files=1 switches the WM firmware to BIN_METHOD with the stock
names (WIFI_MT7993_PATCH_MCU_1_1_hdr.bin and WIFI_RAM_CODE_MT7993_1_1.bin),
which is the same content as the built-in copy, and from there
diag_patch_file / diag_ram_file select any file in /lib/firmware at boot
time - the casan pair included.

Default is off, so the untouched build keeps loading the built-in arrays.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
---
--- a/wlan_hwifi/chips/mt7993/mt7993.c
+++ b/wlan_hwifi/chips/mt7993/mt7993.c
@@ -58,6 +58,18 @@
 module_param(intr_option_set, byte, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(intr_option_set, "Interrupt Option Set");
 
+/*
+ * 057: every image we can test so far is compiled into the driver, so trying
+ * another one costs a full build.  With this set the WM firmware is requested
+ * from /lib/firmware instead, which makes diag_patch_file/diag_ram_file - and
+ * therefore every variant shipped in the image, casan included - switchable
+ * from /etc/modules.d at boot time.
+ */
+static bool diag_use_fw_files;
+module_param(diag_use_fw_files, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(diag_use_fw_files,
+		 "load the WM patch and RAM code from /lib/firmware instead of the built-in header");
+
 static u8 rro_mode = HW_RRO_V3_1;
 module_param(rro_mode, byte, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(rro_mode, "RRO Mode");
@@ -1737,6 +1749,22 @@
 	mcu_info->fw_hdr_len[MCU_FW_MODE_TESTMODE] = sizeof(mt7993_FirmwareImage_Testmode_1_1);
 	mcu_info->rom_patch_hdr = mt7993_rom_patch_1_1;
 	mcu_info->applied_method = HEADER_METHOD;
+
+	if (diag_use_fw_files) {
+		/*
+		 * BIN_METHOD makes mcu_wm load the two images with
+		 * request_firmware(); give it the stock names so a plain
+		 * diag_use_fw_files=1 behaves exactly like the built-in copy
+		 * and only diag_patch_file/diag_ram_file change it.
+		 */
+		mcu_info->fw_patch = MT7993_ROM_PATCH;
+		mcu_info->fw_ram[MCU_FW_MODE_NORMALMODE] = MT7993_FIRMWARE_WM;
+		mcu_info->fw_ram[MCU_FW_MODE_TESTMODE] =
+			MT7993_FIRMWARE_WM_TESTMODE;
+		mcu_info->applied_method = BIN_METHOD;
+		pr_err("diag: WM firmware from /lib/firmware (%s, %s)\n",
+		       MT7993_ROM_PATCH, MT7993_FIRMWARE_WM);
+	}
 }
 #endif /* CONFIG_HWIFI_FW_HDR_SUPPORT */
 
